          "date": "2026-08-22T21:14:55Z",
          "message": "serve the PCR lineage (cycle 250) on the site\n\ndocs/models_9x9/best.onnx now comes from runs/models_9x9_pcr/best.pt instead\nof the scratch lineage. Measured at 800 sims, 300 games/pair: pcr 250 beats\npcr 220 81.5% and the previously-served scratch 321 85.5%. pcr 220 had already\ntaken rank 1 in pcr_ab v3 (60.7%, beating scratch 321 70.1% over 600 games).\n\nScratch 321 stays browsable in the picker as checkpoints/scratch_0321.onnx.\nThree 9x9 lineages now share docs/models_9x9/checkpoints/, so bare\ncycle_NNNN.onnx is reserved for the heads auto-glob and one-off exports from\nother lineages carry a lineage prefix; modelShortLabel renders those too.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "url": "https://github.com/bartolomeo3000/SigmaQuoridor/commit/751186344fc52ad0c29bc65922e62c6fa915f006"
        },
        {
          "sha": "a7a91e5e8ccb561b9e520bc96a1c199a0f16ab12",
          "date": "2026-07-25T14:57:59Z",
          "message": "restructure repo: runs/ for artifacts, drop the RL track, serve the scratch net\n\nLayout\n------\nAll generated artifacts move under runs/ (model lineages, self-play data,\ntournament results, logs), leaving 8 directories at the repo root instead of\n18. Source stays at the root -- docs/ is pinned there by GitHub Pages, and the\nquoridor_cpp extension is built in-place, so a src/ layout would have cost more\nthan it bought. Paths are cwd-relative, so run everything from the repo root.\n\nTwo things a string-level path rewrite could not fix:\n\n  * cpp_train_loop.py inferred the data dir from basename() alone, so\n    runs/models_9x9_scratch resolved to a top-level data_9x9_scratch that no\n    longer exists -- it would have self-played into a fresh empty directory\n    instead of failing. Now keeps the parent, matching train.py.\n  * Tournament CSVs store model paths as roster names, and --baseline matches\n    pairs on those exact strings. They were rewritten in place (30 files) so\n    series inheritance and game reuse keep working; without it, extending the\n    series would have silently replayed all 91 pairs.\n\nTournament series\n-----------------\ntournament_cpp.py gains --series/--add: it reads the previous version's own\nfiles (vN.csv for the roster and games/pair, vN_matchups.csv as the baseline,\nthe .meta.json sidecar for the rules config) instead of making the caller\nretype 18 lines of flags. Deriving from those files rather than a separate\nmanifest keeps one source of truth. Roster de-duplication compares normalised\npaths, so an --add with forward slashes cannot register an already-present\nmodel a second time.\n\nRL baseline track removed\n-------------------------\nrl_models.py and friends were deleted, which left app.py failing to import.\nRemoved the Flask agent registry, the browser app's Simple RL option and\nworker branch, and docs/models/simple_rl/.\n\nModel serving\n-------------\ndocs/models_9x9/best.onnx is now the from-scratch lineage's cycle 321, which\nbeat the old heads cycle 56 head-to-head (61.1% over 500 games) and took rank 1\nin the v7 tournament. Heads cycle 56 stays as checkpoints/cycle_0056.onnx for\ncomparison; the other 23 stale checkpoint exports are gone (277MB -> 23MB).\n\nAlso: training_stats.csv now records self-play time. cycle_time_s only ever\ncovered training, because cpp_train_loop.py runs self-play in a separate\nsubprocess -- 8.4h of a real 35.7h. Self-play wall time is passed through to\ntrain.py, and the history was reconstructed from the self-play logs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "url": "https://github.com/bartolomeo3000/SigmaQuoridor/commit/a7a91e5e8ccb561b9e520bc96a1c199a0f16ab12"
        },
